// SIMS — Savemore Investigation Management System — schema v2
//
// Conventions
//  - Internal ids are CUIDs. Business references (SIMS/2026/0001 …) are separate, unique and immutable.
//  - Money is Decimal(18,2). Never Float.
//  - isDemo marks fictional seed data (shown as DEMO DATA in the UI).
//  - `version` supports optimistic locking on rows edited by several people.
//  - Business tables carry the soft-delete block (isDeleted … restorationReason) and archivedAt.
//    Lists exclude deleted rows unless the Recycle Bin asks for them.
//  - Rows that must never be silently changed (audit logs, evidence originals, custody records,
//    verified recoveries) are protected by database triggers (see the guards migration).
//  - MariaDB sizing: Prisma maps a bare String to VARCHAR(191). Every free-text column carries an
//    explicit @db.VarChar(n) / @db.Text / @db.MediumText at least as large as its validation limit
//    (the registry `max`, or the route's Zod schema), so valid input is never truncated.
//  - Lists of strings are Json columns holding string[] (MariaDB has no array type). They are read
//    and written whole; the only database-side filter is the statement-scoped `flags` lookup.

generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client-js"
}

datasource db {
  // MariaDB 10.11 on the production host (Prisma's MySQL connector). See docs/MYSQL-MIGRATION-PLAN.md.
  provider = "mysql"
  url      = env("DATABASE_URL")
}

